WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.733
Every number you need, live, as you pedal.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.928
Power leads. The bike reports none, so Wattzup estimates it from cadence and

00:00:12.928 --> 00:00:15.109
resistance, and marks it est.

00:00:15.309 --> 00:00:19.712
Three seventeen watts, against a target of three twenty-seven: on target.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.273
Push harder, and it reads plus one ninety-four watts.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.282
Ease off, and minus one eighty-five.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:36.898
Cadence sits beside it, with the segment's aim: ninety-five, aim for ninety-eight.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:47.194
Underneath, the ride totals: average power, speed in kilometres and miles an hour,

00:00:47.194 --> 00:00:48.761
distance and energy.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:57.333
With no workout, it's a free ride: no target, no cadence goal, and Set up a ride one

00:00:57.333 --> 00:00:58.204
tap away.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:05.385
On a phone or a tablet, the same numbers lead the screen.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:16.230
What the tests prove: on target means within eight percent of the target.

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:20.838
And the totals stay on screen after the ride ends, until the next one starts.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:28.546
That is journey three. Wattzup turns an Echelon bike or treadmill into a live

00:01:28.546 --> 00:01:29.850
training display.
